WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:15.687
Acting on instinct, Zann rubbed his hands together.

2
00:00:15.688 --> 00:00:17.005
"Decelerate!"

3
00:00:17.006 --> 00:00:23.223
Zann immediately felt himself slow down. Soon he was drifting down no faster than a leaf.

4
00:00:23.224 --> 00:00:31.152
"It's a good thing we just got tested on deceleration in Safety Spells class," he thought as he landed gently on the palace roof.

5
00:00:31.153 --> 00:00:34.491
"Zann!" someone shouted from far overhead.

6
00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:38.080
Zann's friends were still trying to evade the wild dragons.

7
00:00:38.081 --> 00:00:43.474
Fala was attempting to steer her dragon closer to him, but the thunder chargers kept blocking her.

8
00:00:43.475 --> 00:00:48.771
"Go!" Zann shouted, using a Sound-Shifting spell to carry his words to her.

9
00:00:48.772 --> 00:00:52.696
"It's too risky. I'll meet you back in the woods!"

10
00:00:52.697 --> 00:00:56.761
"Are you sure?" Fala sent her words back to Zann the same way.

11
00:00:56.762 --> 00:00:59.464
Zann nodded and gave her a thumbs-up.

12
00:00:59.465 --> 00:01:03.256
Fala and Darb steered the cloud gliders back toward the forest.

13
00:01:03.257 --> 00:01:08.247
The wild dragons chased them for a while and then stopped, disappearing into the clouds.

14
00:01:08.248 --> 00:01:12.951
Knowing that his friends were safe, Zann looked around for a way into the palace.

15
00:01:12.952 --> 00:01:16.058
He was standing on the apex of a steep roof.

16
00:01:16.059 --> 00:01:20.150
Looking down he could see the top of a small dormer jutting out.

17
00:01:20.151 --> 00:01:23.510
"Maybe there's a window on that dormer," he thought.

18
00:01:23.511 --> 00:01:29.182
Zann was nervous about using any more magic than he needed to—especially with Morb so close.

19
00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:34.047
Keeping himself as flat as he could, he inched his way down slowly.

20
00:01:34.048 --> 00:01:37.819
When Zann was about halfway down, he lost his grip.

21
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:44.192
"Oh no!" he cried, sliding fast. Zann could see the edge of the roof quickly getting closer.

22
00:01:44.193 --> 00:01:47.598
He slid past the dormer and then he was in midair.

23
00:01:47.599 --> 00:01:49.956
Zann cried out, "Decelerate—"

24
00:01:49.957 --> 00:01:51.899
Bam!

25
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:56.064
"Ouch!" Zann looked at the small balcony he'd just landed on.

26
00:01:56.065 --> 00:02:01.622
Then he saw the door. With a sigh of relief, he got up and headed into the palace.

27
00:02:01.623 --> 00:02:05.997
Morb and Slib walked down the cracked steps of the ancient staircase.

28
00:02:05.998 --> 00:02:11.551
"This is what you call a dungeon?" said Morb, wrinkling his nose at the awful smell.

29
00:02:11.552 --> 00:02:19.997
Slib bowed. "Forgive me, Your Highness. It hasn't been used since the Old Times."

30
00:02:19.998 --> 00:02:28.029
The place was a mess. The stone walls were cracked and crumbling, many of the iron bars were either missing or badly rusted,

31
00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:31.842
and everything was coated in a thick layer of dust.

32
00:02:31.843 --> 00:02:41.362
"A few Voids have already arrived in response to your invitation," Slib went on in that servile tone that Morb already found annoying.

33
00:02:41.363 --> 00:02:46.046
"Perhaps we could put them to work cleaning and repairing this place."

34
00:02:46.047 --> 00:02:54.907
Morb shot him a sharp look. "Is that all you think Voids are good for?" he demanded. "Cleaning up others' messes?"

35
00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:59.363
Slib looked confused. "I only meant—"

36
00:02:59.364 --> 00:03:04.450
Morb didn't let him finish. "How many Reds have turned themselves in so far?"

37
00:03:04.451 --> 00:03:08.541
Slib's expression changed to nervousness. "Uh . . ."

38
00:03:08.542 --> 00:03:10.249
"How many?"

39
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:16.953
"None, Your Majesty," Slib said. "But that's typical of Reds, isn't it?

40
00:03:16.954 --> 00:03:21.372
Always thinking they're too good to follow the rules."

41
00:03:21.373 --> 00:03:28.548
Morb gnashed his teeth. He was so furious that he almost struck Slib down with a Blast spell.

42
00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:33.659
"Never mind," Morb muttered. "Soon it won't matter."

43
00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.083
"Pardon me, Your Majesty?" said Slib.

44
00:03:37.084 --> 00:03:40.560
Morb glanced at him. "Stand back," he ordered.

45
00:03:40.561 --> 00:03:44.218
Touching his fingertips together, Morb pointed at the dungeon.

46
00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:48.587
The walls quickly rebuilt themselves out of the rubble.

47
00:03:48.588 --> 00:03:54.467
Strong iron bars grew out of the hard stone floor and formed new cell doors.

48
00:03:54.468 --> 00:04:00.782
Slib gasped. "Your Majesty!" he exclaimed. "Such power!"

49
00:04:00.783 --> 00:04:07.279
Morb ignored him. Closing his eyes, he summoned up the energy for a much more difficult task.

50
00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.715
"Come to me," he murmured. Zap!

51
00:04:12.716 --> 00:04:17.790
In a flash all the Red prisoners from the fortress appeared in the cells.

52
00:04:17.791 --> 00:04:24.400
Morb hardly heard Slib's exclamations this time, or the cries of the surprised prisoners either.

53
00:04:24.401 --> 00:04:29.441
He'd used up much of his energy last night, and this task had drained him again.

54
00:04:29.442 --> 00:04:32.534
He would need another magic infusion soon.

55
00:04:32.535 --> 00:04:41.336
"Slib," he ordered hoarsely, holding onto a pillar for support, "tell the trolls to bring more leeches immediately."

56
00:04:41.337 --> 00:04:48.033
Slib gulped. "Your Highness," he said, "there aren't many leeches left.

57
00:04:48.034 --> 00:04:50.967
You used most of them last night."

58
00:04:50.968 --> 00:04:54.109
"Just bring them to me," commanded Morb.

59
00:04:54.110 --> 00:05:02.117
In order to restore himself the night before, Morb had been forced to use almost all of his leeches on the non-Reds in the palace.

60
00:05:02.118 --> 00:05:08.483
As soon as the old woman arrived with his sea sponge, he would have to send her out for more leeches.

61
00:05:08.484 --> 00:05:13.748
"Are you okay, little buddy?" Darb asked, peeling Zing loose from the cloud glider's back.

62
00:05:13.749 --> 00:05:18.420
The fire whistler had been hanging on for dear life the whole way back to the forest.

63
00:05:18.421 --> 00:05:21.983
"Never mind him," Perda said. "What about Zann?"

64
00:05:21.984 --> 00:05:26.878
Fala slid down from her dragon. "He told us to go," she said.

65
00:05:26.879 --> 00:05:30.754
"We never would have gotten past those thunder chargers anyway.

66
00:05:30.755 --> 00:05:34.931
Zann can take care of himself—he'll get out of the palace."

67
00:05:34.932 --> 00:05:38.269
Perda glanced around. "How will he find us?

68
00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.027
We must be miles from where we started.

69
00:05:41.028 --> 00:05:43.933
Maybe we should fly back to the original spot."

70
00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:49.683
But one look at the exhausted cloud gliders told Perda that that wasn't practical right now.

71
00:05:49.684 --> 00:05:52.425
"We should at least send him a message moth."

72
00:05:52.426 --> 00:05:56.183
"Good idea." Fala snapped her fingers to summon a moth.

73
00:05:56.184 --> 00:05:58.898
After scribbling a message, she released it.

74
00:05:58.899 --> 00:06:02.345
It was midday by now, and it was getting hot.

75
00:06:02.346 --> 00:06:06.500
Perda wandered toward a shadier spot with the others trailing behind her.

76
00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:11.823
Suddenly Perda felt magical energy surround her as she was lifted into the air.

77
00:06:11.824 --> 00:06:16.885
"Hey!" she shouted. She struggled against the magic, but it was useless.

78
00:06:16.886 --> 00:06:19.645
She could see that her friends were being lifted as well.

79
00:06:19.646 --> 00:06:29.380
"Do not try to resist," a voice commanded from somewhere in the forest. "You're surrounded."
